<title>UK: Low cotton prices prompt selective European buying.</title>
<headline>Low cotton prices prompt selective European buying.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, ENGLAND 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asking prices for selected upland cottons were pitched at competitively low prices for first and second quarter delivery 1997, industry sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Best quality West African grades and some Central Africans featured strongly, seeing modest volumes traded in what has otherwise been a neglected market.</p>
<p>The 'A' Index ended at 75.50, unchanged since Monday.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
